// Typechecks everything tsconfig.json builds, plus the test files and the
// test helpers that it excludes. `npm run typecheck` uses this one; the build
// still uses tsconfig.json, so nothing test-shaped reaches dist.
//
// The `exclude` below is the whole point and the easy thing to get wrong.
// tsconfig `exclude` REPLACES the inherited array rather than merging with it.
// Leave it out and this file silently inherits
//   ["src/**/*.test.ts", "src/testing/**"]
// from the parent: the config looks wired up, `typecheck` exits 0, and not one
// extra line is checked. That is the failure shape of this whole week, a check
// that appears to run and is looking at the wrong thing.
//
// This package excluded two things, so lifting both was a second decision.
// The helpers under src/testing are in, deliberately. fake-claude.ts is the
// file whose unnarrowed ToolUnion read produced 22 of the 30 errors found when
// the exclusion came off, and a helper every test leans on is the last thing
// that should be exempt from checking.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noEmit": true },
  "exclude": ["dist"]
}
